# Beads Issue Tracking

This project uses [beads_rust (br)](https://github.com/steveyegge/beads) for issue tracking.

> **Note:** `br` is non-invasive and never executes git commands. After `br sync --flush-only`, you must manually run `git add .beads/ && git commit`.

## Core Rules
- Track ALL work in br (never use markdown TODOs or comment-based task lists)
- Use `br ready` to find available work
- Use `br create` to track new issues/tasks/bugs
- Use `br sync --flush-only` at end of session, then `git add .beads/ && git commit`

## Quick Reference
```bash
br prime                              # Load complete workflow context
br ready                              # Show issues ready to work (no blockers)
br list --status=open                 # List all open issues
br create --title="..." --type=task  # Create new issue
br update <id> --status=in_progress  # Claim work
br close <id>                         # Mark complete
br dep add <issue> <depends-on>       # Add dependency (issue depends on depends-on)
br sync --flush-only                  # Export to JSONL
git add .beads/ && git commit         # Then commit manually
```

## Workflow
1. Check for ready work: `br ready`
2. Claim an issue: `br update <id> --status=in_progress`
3. Do the work
4. Mark complete: `br close <id>`
5. Sync: `br sync --flush-only && git add .beads/ && git commit`

## Context Loading
Run `br prime` to get complete workflow documentation in AI-optimized format (~1-2k tokens).

For detailed docs: see AGENTS.md, QUICKSTART.md, or run `br --help`
